# Dev-only files — excluded from what actually gets uploaded to Cloudflare.
# Same gitignore-style syntax, honored by `wrangler deploy`; the deployed site
# only needs index.html, style.css, script.js, data.js, manifest.json, sw.js,
# robots.txt, sitemap.xml, _headers, assets/, and icons/.
#
# robots.txt and sitemap.xml must NOT be added here — they only do their job
# if crawlers can fetch them from the deployed origin. Same for _headers: it
# has to reach Cloudflare's asset storage for the per-path Cache-Control
# rules in it to take effect at all — Cloudflare reads it, then serves it as
# config rather than as a public file (confirmed: /_headers itself 404s).
#
# This list only matters for a bare `wrangler deploy` run straight from the
# repo root. The real deploy path (`npm run deploy`) never reaches it at
# all — it deploys from dist/, a scripts/build.js output that only ever
# contains the files above in the first place, minified. `scripts` is
# listed below purely as a safety net for that bare-deploy fallback case.
wrangler.jsonc
serve.py
package.json
package-lock.json
scripts
dist
node_modules
.claude
.wrangler
.git
.gitignore
.assetsignore
LICENSE
*.md
